{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"},{"type":"text","value":", …) configuration you want to reuse — across multiple routes, between a server function and its caller, or simply factored out of a handler for clarity. By the end of this guide, you'll have a single typed options object that infers the adapter's model, modalities, and provider options, and that you can spread into any call site without losing type safety."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every activity in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":" ships a paired "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createXxxOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" helper that takes the exact same options object as the activity itself and returns it unchanged — at runtime it's the identity function. The point is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"type inference"}]},{"type":"text","value":": the returned object carries the adapter's full type, so when you spread it into the activity, TypeScript still narrows "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", content modalities, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"outputSchema"},{"type":"text","value":" to the adapter you chose."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { chat, createChatOptions } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatOptions({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  // modelOptions, systemPrompts, tools — all type-checked against the\n  // adapter+model pair above. Sampling params (temperature, top_p,\n  // max_output_tokens, …) live inside modelOptions, under each provider's\n  // native key.\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    reasoning: { effort: 'medium' },\n  },\n})\n\n// Later, anywhere in your codebase:\nconst stream = chat({ ...chatOptions, messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }] })","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without the helper you'd have to either inline the configuration at every call site, or hand-write the full chat options type with its adapter/model generics resolved manually — "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" does that for you."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"when-to-reach-for-it","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When to reach for it"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Sharing a configuration across multiple routes"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — define once, spread into each handler."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Passing options through a layer"}]},{"type":"text","value":" (a server function, a wrapper, a test fixture) without erasing the adapter's model-specific types."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Branching on a runtime value while keeping types intact"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — build different options objects and choose between them, instead of weaving conditionals into a single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat({...})"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Co-locating tools, system prompts, and middleware"}]},{"type":"text","value":" with the adapter they target."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you only call an activity once at one site, you don't need this helper. Inline the options."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"available-helpers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Available helpers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each helper mirrors the activity it pairs with. Same options, same return type."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Helper"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Activity"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Adapter"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"text adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiText"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anthropicText"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSummarizeOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"summarize()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"summarize adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiSummarize"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createImageOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"image adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiImage"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falImage"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAudioOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateAudio()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"audio adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falAudio"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"geminiAudio"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createVideoOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVideo()"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getVideoJobStatus()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"video adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falVideo"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiVideo"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createLiveVideoOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateLiveVideo()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"live adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorVideo"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falLiveVideo"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createWorldOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateWorld()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"world adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"reactorWorld"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"worldlabsWorld"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSpeechOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"speech adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"elevenlabsSpeech"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTranscriptionOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateTranscription()"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"transcription adapter (e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiTranscription"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"falTranscription"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All helpers are exported from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-shared-chat-configuration-across-routes","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: shared chat configuration across routes"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Suppose you have several routes that all hit the same model with the same provider options and tool set. Factor the configuration out once:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// lib/ai/chat-options.ts\nimport { createChatOptions, toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nconst lookupOrderDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'lookupOrder',\n  description: 'Look up a customer order by ID',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ orderId: z.string() }),\n})\n\nconst lookupOrder = lookupOrderDef.server(async ({ orderId }) => {\n  return db.orders.findUnique({ where: { id: orderId } })\n})\n\nexport const supportChatOptions = createChatOptions({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  systemPrompts: ['You are a customer-support assistant for Acme Corp.'],\n  tools: [lookupOrder],\n  modelOptions: {\n    reasoning: { effort: 'medium' },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/support/chat.ts\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { supportChatOptions } from '@/lib/ai/chat-options'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const stream = chat({ ...supportChatOptions, messages })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/support/draft-reply.ts — same adapter+tools, different schema\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { supportChatOptions } from '@/lib/ai/chat-options'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { ticket } = await request.json()\n  const draft = await chat({\n    ...supportChatOptions,\n    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: `Draft a reply to: ${ticket}` }],\n    outputSchema: z.object({ subject: z.string(), body: z.string() }),\n    stream: false,\n  })\n  return Response.json(draft)\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both routes share the adapter, system prompt, tools, and reasoning settings; each adds what it needs. Override or omit any field at the call site — the spread wins on the right."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example-typed-pre-configured-image-generation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example: typed pre-configured image generation"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { createImageOptions, generateImage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst heroImageOptions = createImageOptions({\n  adapter: openaiImage('gpt-image-2'),\n  prompt: 'A glass sphere refracting a sunset over a calm sea',\n  size: '1536x1024',\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n})\n\nconst result = await generateImage(heroImageOptions)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same pattern works for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createVideoOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSpeechOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTranscriptionOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createAudioOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createSummarizeOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" — the adapter is captured in the typed options object and every downstream call is narrowed to it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-the-helper-does-not-do","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the helper does NOT do"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No runtime behavior."}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createChatOptions(opts)"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"opts"},{"type":"text","value":". There is no validation, freezing, cloning, or memoization. If you mutate the returned object after creation, the next call sees the mutation. Treat the result as immutable by convention."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No partial typing."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The helper expects the full options shape it'll be spread into. If you need to build options up incrementally, type the intermediate state yourself (a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Partial<>"},{"type":"text","value":" of the full chat options shape) and only call the helper at the boundary where the shape is complete."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No request execution."}]},{"type":"text","value":" The helper does not call the model. Only the activity function ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"chat"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateImage"},{"type":"text","value":", …) makes the request."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"related","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Related"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./per-model-type-safety","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Per-Model Type Safety"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — how the adapter+model pair drives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" inference."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./tree-shaking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tree-Shaking"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — why each adapter is exported separately, and how the typed-options pattern keeps your bundle small."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"./extend-adapter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Extend Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" — when you need to add custom models to an adapter without losing the same typed-options ergonomics."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"the-pattern","text":"The pattern","level":2},{"id":"when-to-reach-for-it","text":"When to reach for it","level":2},{"id":"available-helpers","text":"Available helpers","level":2},{"id":"example-shared-chat-configuration-across-routes","text":"Example: shared chat configuration across routes","level":2},{"id":"example-typed-pre-configured-image-generation","text":"Example: typed pre-configured image generation","level":2},{"id":"what-the-helper-does-not-do","text":"What the helper does NOT do","level":2},{"id":"related","text":"Related","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a `chat()` (or `generateImage()`, `generateSpeech()`, …) configuration you want to reuse — across multiple routes, between a server function and its caller, or simply factored out of a handler for clarity. By the end of this guide, you'll have a single typed options object that infers the adapter's model, modalities, and provider options, and that you can spread into any call site without losing type safety.\n\n## The pattern\n\nEvery activity in `@tanstack/ai` ships a paired `createXxxOptions` helper that takes the exact same options object as the activity itself and returns it unchanged — at runtime it's the identity function. The point is **type inference**: the returned object carries the adapter's full type, so when you spread it into the activity, TypeScript still narrows `modelOptions`, content modalities, and `outputSchema` to the adapter you chose.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, createChatOptions } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatOptions({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  // modelOptions, systemPrompts, tools — all type-checked against the\n  // adapter+model pair above. Sampling params (temperature, top_p,\n  // max_output_tokens, …) live inside modelOptions, under each provider's\n  // native key.\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    reasoning: { effort: 'medium' },\n  },\n})\n\n// Later, anywhere in your codebase:\nconst stream = chat({ ...chatOptions, messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }] })\n```\n\nWithout the helper you'd have to either inline the configuration at every call site, or hand-write the full chat options type with its adapter/model generics resolved manually — `createChatOptions` does that for you.\n\n## When to reach for it\n\n- **Sharing a configuration across multiple routes** — define once, spread into each handler.\n- **Passing options through a layer** (a server function, a wrapper, a test fixture) without erasing the adapter's model-specific types.\n- **Branching on a runtime value while keeping types intact** — build different options objects and choose between them, instead of weaving conditionals into a single `chat({...})` call.\n- **Co-locating tools, system prompts, and middleware** with the adapter they target.\n\nIf you only call an activity once at one site, you don't need this helper. Inline the options.\n\n## Available helpers\n\nEach helper mirrors the activity it pairs with. Same options, same return type.\n\n| Helper | Activity | Adapter |\n|---|---|---|\n| `createChatOptions` | `chat()` | text adapter (e.g. `openaiText`, `anthropicText`) |\n| `createSummarizeOptions` | `summarize()` | summarize adapter (e.g. `openaiSummarize`) |\n| `createImageOptions` | `generateImage()` | image adapter (e.g. `openaiImage`, `falImage`) |\n| `createAudioOptions` | `generateAudio()` | audio adapter (e.g. `falAudio`, `geminiAudio`) |\n| `createVideoOptions` | `generateVideo()` / `getVideoJobStatus()` | video adapter (e.g. `falVideo`, `openaiVideo`) |\n| `createLiveVideoOptions` | `generateLiveVideo()` | live adapter (e.g. `reactorVideo`, `falLiveVideo`) |\n| `createWorldOptions` | `generateWorld()` | world adapter (e.g. `reactorWorld`, `worldlabsWorld`) |\n| `createSpeechOptions` | `generateSpeech()` | speech adapter (e.g. `openaiSpeech`, `elevenlabsSpeech`) |\n| `createTranscriptionOptions` | `generateTranscription()` | transcription adapter (e.g. `openaiTranscription`, `falTranscription`) |\n\nAll helpers are exported from `@tanstack/ai`.\n\n## Example: shared chat configuration across routes\n\nSuppose you have several routes that all hit the same model with the same provider options and tool set. Factor the configuration out once:\n\n```typescript\n// lib/ai/chat-options.ts\nimport { createChatOptions, toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nconst lookupOrderDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'lookupOrder',\n  description: 'Look up a customer order by ID',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ orderId: z.string() }),\n})\n\nconst lookupOrder = lookupOrderDef.server(async ({ orderId }) => {\n  return db.orders.findUnique({ where: { id: orderId } })\n})\n\nexport const supportChatOptions = createChatOptions({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  systemPrompts: ['You are a customer-support assistant for Acme Corp.'],\n  tools: [lookupOrder],\n  modelOptions: {\n    reasoning: { effort: 'medium' },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/support/chat.ts\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { supportChatOptions } from '@/lib/ai/chat-options'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const stream = chat({ ...supportChatOptions, messages })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/support/draft-reply.ts — same adapter+tools, different schema\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { supportChatOptions } from '@/lib/ai/chat-options'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { ticket } = await request.json()\n  const draft = await chat({\n    ...supportChatOptions,\n    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: `Draft a reply to: ${ticket}` }],\n    outputSchema: z.object({ subject: z.string(), body: z.string() }),\n    stream: false,\n  })\n  return Response.json(draft)\n}\n```\n\nBoth routes share the adapter, system prompt, tools, and reasoning settings; each adds what it needs. Override or omit any field at the call site — the spread wins on the right.\n\n## Example: typed pre-configured image generation\n\n```typescript\nimport { createImageOptions, generateImage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst heroImageOptions = createImageOptions({\n  adapter: openaiImage('gpt-image-2'),\n  prompt: 'A glass sphere refracting a sunset over a calm sea',\n  size: '1536x1024',\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n})\n\nconst result = await generateImage(heroImageOptions)\n```\n\nThe same pattern works for `createVideoOptions`, `createSpeechOptions`, `createTranscriptionOptions`, `createAudioOptions`, and `createSummarizeOptions` — the adapter is captured in the typed options object and every downstream call is narrowed to it.\n\n## What the helper does NOT do\n\n- **No runtime behavior.** `createChatOptions(opts)` is `opts`. There is no validation, freezing, cloning, or memoization. If you mutate the returned object after creation, the next call sees the mutation. Treat the result as immutable by convention.\n- **No partial typing.** The helper expects the full options shape it'll be spread into. If you need to build options up incrementally, type the intermediate state yourself (a `Partial<>` of the full chat options shape) and only call the helper at the boundary where the shape is complete.\n- **No request execution.** The helper does not call the model. Only the activity function (`chat`, `generateImage`, …) makes the request.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Per-Model Type Safety](./per-model-type-safety) — how the adapter+model pair drives `modelOptions` inference.\n- [Tree-Shaking](./tree-shaking) — why each adapter is exported separately, and how the typed-options pattern keeps your bundle small.\n- [Extend Adapter](./extend-adapter) — when you need to add custom models to an adapter without losing the same typed-options ergonomics.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Typed Pre-Configured Options\nid: typed-options\norder: 11\ndescription: \"Define typed, reusable option objects for chat, summarize, image, video, audio, speech, and transcription with createChatOptions and friends — share configuration across routes without losing per-model type safety.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - createChatOptions\n  - createSummarizeOptions\n  - createImageOptions\n  - createSpeechOptions\n  - createTranscriptionOptions\n  - createAudioOptions\n  - createVideoOptions\n  - typed options\n  - shared configuration\n---\n\nYou have a `chat()` (or `generateImage()`, `generateSpeech()`, …) configuration you want to reuse — across multiple routes, between a server function and its caller, or simply factored out of a handler for clarity. By the end of this guide, you'll have a single typed options object that infers the adapter's model, modalities, and provider options, and that you can spread into any call site without losing type safety.\n\n## The pattern\n\nEvery activity in `@tanstack/ai` ships a paired `createXxxOptions` helper that takes the exact same options object as the activity itself and returns it unchanged — at runtime it's the identity function. The point is **type inference**: the returned object carries the adapter's full type, so when you spread it into the activity, TypeScript still narrows `modelOptions`, content modalities, and `outputSchema` to the adapter you chose.\n\n```typescript\nimport { chat, createChatOptions } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst chatOptions = createChatOptions({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  // modelOptions, systemPrompts, tools — all type-checked against the\n  // adapter+model pair above. Sampling params (temperature, top_p,\n  // max_output_tokens, …) live inside modelOptions, under each provider's\n  // native key.\n  modelOptions: {\n    temperature: 0.3,\n    reasoning: { effort: 'medium' },\n  },\n})\n\n// Later, anywhere in your codebase:\nconst stream = chat({ ...chatOptions, messages: [{ role: 'user', content: 'Hello' }] })\n```\n\nWithout the helper you'd have to either inline the configuration at every call site, or hand-write the full chat options type with its adapter/model generics resolved manually — `createChatOptions` does that for you.\n\n## When to reach for it\n\n- **Sharing a configuration across multiple routes** — define once, spread into each handler.\n- **Passing options through a layer** (a server function, a wrapper, a test fixture) without erasing the adapter's model-specific types.\n- **Branching on a runtime value while keeping types intact** — build different options objects and choose between them, instead of weaving conditionals into a single `chat({...})` call.\n- **Co-locating tools, system prompts, and middleware** with the adapter they target.\n\nIf you only call an activity once at one site, you don't need this helper. Inline the options.\n\n## Available helpers\n\nEach helper mirrors the activity it pairs with. Same options, same return type.\n\n| Helper | Activity | Adapter |\n|---|---|---|\n| `createChatOptions` | `chat()` | text adapter (e.g. `openaiText`, `anthropicText`) |\n| `createSummarizeOptions` | `summarize()` | summarize adapter (e.g. `openaiSummarize`) |\n| `createImageOptions` | `generateImage()` | image adapter (e.g. `openaiImage`, `falImage`) |\n| `createAudioOptions` | `generateAudio()` | audio adapter (e.g. `falAudio`, `geminiAudio`) |\n| `createVideoOptions` | `generateVideo()` / `getVideoJobStatus()` | video adapter (e.g. `falVideo`, `openaiVideo`) |\n| `createLiveVideoOptions` | `generateLiveVideo()` | live adapter (e.g. `reactorVideo`, `falLiveVideo`) |\n| `createWorldOptions` | `generateWorld()` | world adapter (e.g. `reactorWorld`, `worldlabsWorld`) |\n| `createSpeechOptions` | `generateSpeech()` | speech adapter (e.g. `openaiSpeech`, `elevenlabsSpeech`) |\n| `createTranscriptionOptions` | `generateTranscription()` | transcription adapter (e.g. `openaiTranscription`, `falTranscription`) |\n\nAll helpers are exported from `@tanstack/ai`.\n\n## Example: shared chat configuration across routes\n\nSuppose you have several routes that all hit the same model with the same provider options and tool set. Factor the configuration out once:\n\n```typescript\n// lib/ai/chat-options.ts\nimport { createChatOptions, toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\nimport { db } from './db'\n\nconst lookupOrderDef = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'lookupOrder',\n  description: 'Look up a customer order by ID',\n  inputSchema: z.object({ orderId: z.string() }),\n})\n\nconst lookupOrder = lookupOrderDef.server(async ({ orderId }) => {\n  return db.orders.findUnique({ where: { id: orderId } })\n})\n\nexport const supportChatOptions = createChatOptions({\n  adapter: openaiText('gpt-5.5'),\n  systemPrompts: ['You are a customer-support assistant for Acme Corp.'],\n  tools: [lookupOrder],\n  modelOptions: {\n    reasoning: { effort: 'medium' },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/support/chat.ts\nimport { chat, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { supportChatOptions } from '@/lib/ai/chat-options'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { messages } = await request.json()\n  const stream = chat({ ...supportChatOptions, messages })\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n}\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/support/draft-reply.ts — same adapter+tools, different schema\nimport { chat } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { supportChatOptions } from '@/lib/ai/chat-options'\nimport { z } from 'zod'\n\nexport async function POST(request: Request) {\n  const { ticket } = await request.json()\n  const draft = await chat({\n    ...supportChatOptions,\n    messages: [{ role: 'user', content: `Draft a reply to: ${ticket}` }],\n    outputSchema: z.object({ subject: z.string(), body: z.string() }),\n    stream: false,\n  })\n  return Response.json(draft)\n}\n```\n\nBoth routes share the adapter, system prompt, tools, and reasoning settings; each adds what it needs. Override or omit any field at the call site — the spread wins on the right.\n\n## Example: typed pre-configured image generation\n\n```typescript\nimport { createImageOptions, generateImage } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiImage } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\n\nconst heroImageOptions = createImageOptions({\n  adapter: openaiImage('gpt-image-2'),\n  prompt: 'A glass sphere refracting a sunset over a calm sea',\n  size: '1536x1024',\n  numberOfImages: 1,\n})\n\nconst result = await generateImage(heroImageOptions)\n```\n\nThe same pattern works for `createVideoOptions`, `createSpeechOptions`, `createTranscriptionOptions`, `createAudioOptions`, and `createSummarizeOptions` — the adapter is captured in the typed options object and every downstream call is narrowed to it.\n\n## What the helper does NOT do\n\n- **No runtime behavior.** `createChatOptions(opts)` is `opts`. There is no validation, freezing, cloning, or memoization. If you mutate the returned object after creation, the next call sees the mutation. Treat the result as immutable by convention.\n- **No partial typing.** The helper expects the full options shape it'll be spread into. If you need to build options up incrementally, type the intermediate state yourself (a `Partial<>` of the full chat options shape) and only call the helper at the boundary where the shape is complete.\n- **No request execution.** The helper does not call the model. Only the activity function (`chat`, `generateImage`, …) makes the request.\n\n## Related\n\n- [Per-Model Type Safety](./per-model-type-safety) — how the adapter+model pair drives `modelOptions` inference.\n- [Tree-Shaking](./tree-shaking) — why each adapter is exported separately, and how the typed-options pattern keeps your bundle small.\n- [Extend Adapter](./extend-adapter) — when you need to add custom models to an adapter without losing the same typed-options ergonomics.\n"}
